  "format": "news",
  "script": "The three biggest apps on your phone just put out a price list.\n\nIt's called Meta One, live everywhere this week.\n\nFirst, Instagram Plus and Facebook Plus cost three ninety-nine a month, and WhatsApp Plus runs two ninety-nine.\n\nThen there's Meta AI itself: Core is seven ninety-nine, and Premium is nineteen ninety-nine, for more generation and longer reasoning on hard questions.\n\nNot to mention, business pages climb even higher: Max hits four hundred ninety-nine dollars a month.\n\nHere's why: this kind of AI is expensive to run. Meta poured fourteen point three billion dollars into Scale AI chasing compute, and it wants its heaviest users to help cover the bill.\n\nNow, Meta says the free version isn't going anywhere. This is all extra, not a replacement.\n\nBut look at the cheapest app on that whole list: it's WhatsApp.\n\nThis is the same WhatsApp whose founders built the company on one promise: no ads, no games, no gimmicks. They kept the note on their desk.\n\nLast year, WhatsApp broke that promise and started running ads. This week, it's charging you directly too.\n\nSimply put, free was never permanent. It was only phase one.\n\nComment META and I'll break down which tier's actually worth paying for.",
